      "Chapter 16 — A practical note for operators in India\nThe source does not discuss India-specific implementation. The following is a general checklist to investigate, not legal or tax advice.",
      "If you are based in India and work with a creator in India or overseas, clarify:\n- Whether you are operating as an individual, proprietorship, partnership, LLP, or company.\n- How the creator and operator will invoice or account for their share.\n- Whether GST registration or other tax obligations apply to the business and transaction.\n- How income from overseas clients or platforms should be reported.\n- Whether the payment provider supports your business type, country, currency, and payout arrangement.\n- Whether foreign-exchange and cross-border payment rules apply.\n- Who is responsible for consumer complaints, refunds, and chargebacks.\n- How customer information is collected, stored, and used.\n- Whether the product category has special regulatory requirements.\nDo not assume a US-focused payment platform or split-payment feature is available to an Indian operator. Confirm eligibility and current requirements directly with the provider and a qualified local professional.\nPart 7 — Ready-to-Use Operating Templates"
